# Bug #35 (reported by the user): backend/ accumulated 86 one-off debug/verification scripts
# from earlier development sessions (checksecret.py, checkdburl.py, fixlogin.py, diag.py, and
# similar - none of them part of the actual application), committed alongside main.py with no
# .dockerignore in place to filter them out. The Dockerfile's "COPY . ." (see Dockerfile)
# copies the ENTIRE build context with no filtering, so every one of those scripts baked
# straight into the production image - confirmed decisively: 89 .py files under backend/, only
# 3 of which (main.py and the two test_*.py suites) are real application code.
# Impact beyond image bloat: some of these scripts print or write out real internal
# implementation details - e.g. one dumps the full body of _check_user_auth() to a result
# file, another checks whether DATABASE_URL is set - and one even has a hardcoded local
# Windows path to this project baked in. None of that belongs in a container image that could
# ever be pushed to a registry, inspected via `docker save`/layer analysis, or reached via
# `docker exec`.
# This does not change anything the application needs: main.py imports nothing from these
# scripts (they were never part of its own import graph), so excluding them changes nothing
# about how the app runs - decisively confirmed by starting the full test suite and the
# FastAPI app itself with none of these files present (see the verification done alongside
# this fix).
*.py
!main.py
!test_*.py
*_result.txt
*.diff
*.txt
!requirements.txt
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
